\tag{fdip}
\title{The two first-loop expectations}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A loop transport can be traced on the coefficient
fiber or placed between a barred and an unbarred field.
The fiber-trace insertion formula of \ref{fdip-00WG} relates
the second operation to the inverse kernel. The
#{15} classes above make both averages finite rational
sums.}

